  "Foscarnet is a pyrophosphate analog that inhibits viral DNA polymerase directly, without needing any activating kinase. Because UL97 or DNA polymerase mutations that cause ganciclovir or acyclovir resistance do not necessarily block foscarnet, it is a key option for resistant CMV and acyclovir-resistant HSV, at the cost of nephrotoxicity and electrolyte disturbances.",
